<!--Post: 424--><!--Time: 1089590342-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 11, 2004 - 4:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->According to a 1978 story from the Wichita <i>Eagle-Beacon</i>, as well as statements from the Wichita police, BTK&#39;s first communication was an October 1974 letter sent to the <i>Eagle-Beacon&#39;s</i> &#34;Secret Witness Program.&#34; However, information revealed on the recent episode of <i>Dateline NBC</i> contradicts that widely-held belief. <BR> <BR>Joseph and Julie Otero, along with two of their children, had been strangled in their Wichita home on January 15, 1974. According to <i>Dateline NBC</i>, the Wichita Police Dept. placed a classified ad in the <i>Eagle-Beacon</i> on January 20, 1974. &#40;The ad was shown during the show, along with the front page of the newspaper revealing the date.&#41; The text of the ad is as follows: <BR> <BR><b>B.T.K. <BR>Help is available <BR>Call 684-6321 before 10 p.m.</b> <BR> <BR>If the date of the ad given by <i>Dateline NBC</i> is accurate, BTK must have made contact with either the newspaper or police within a few days of the Otero murders. Furthermore, he must have provided his chosen moniker: BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 424-->
<!--Post: 435--><!--Time: 1089662812-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST435"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 12, 2004 - 1:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom,  <BR> <BR>I have the actual article in front of me. It was in &#34;The Wichita Sun&#34; The ad was placed in the Sun on December 11, 1974. There is an op/ed letter from the Sun explaining why they broke the story about the BTK letter also on Dec. 11, 1974. <BR> <BR>I will quote the important parts.: <BR> <BR>&#34;Thus, The Wichita Sun has determined to publish this weeks controversial front page story concerning the Otero murder case and letter from a man claiming to have killed the four victims. The paper feels that after some months under wraps, this letter should be made public for two separate , but equally important reasons: the community&#39;s right to know and the possibility that The Sun&#39;s comprehensive circulation and the letter&#39;s content could bring forth further information on the case. <BR> <BR>The decision to publicize this latest developement in one of Wichita&#39;s most bizarre multiple homicides came only after much consideration, and a great deal of research as to the authenticy of the document. <BR> <BR>In an effort not to hinder the on-going investigation of the case, the Sun has not published portions of the unsigned &#34;confession&#34; which contained hitherto unrevealed details of the crime - knowledge which evidently could only be had by the killer himself. <BR> <BR>Similarly, the code letters BTK have been left undefined, so that the police can make use of those initials as a test for any future suspects claiming guilt. <BR> <BR>The Sun urges anyone with the info to contact the WPD directly at 262-2611. Detective Maj. Bill Cornwell is in charge of the investigation...&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR>Another Sun article on December 11, 1974: <BR> <BR>&#34;Police refuse to comment on the letter and the confusion remains as to when it was receeved. Although Hannon said this week the letter was received, &#34;three months ago&#34;, the first of the three suspects referred to in the letter was not picked up until Oct. 8 and the third man was not picked up until Oct. 18, eight weeks ago. And it was not until Oct. 24th that police placed a personal classified advertisement in an attempt to contact BTK. Those code letters are not the person&#39;s initials, but are derived from the letterwriter&#39;s characterization of his method of operation.&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR>Hope this helps. Sorry if mistakes in spelling. I typed in a hurry. <BR> <BR>Jaden<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 435-->
<!--Post: 436--><!--Time: 1089664345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST436"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 12, 2004 - 1:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jaden: The premise of this thread is -- based on what was shown on Dateline NBC -- BTK communicated with &#40;most likely&#41; the police within a few days of the Otero murders. In other words, it was <i>before</i> his first known letter and <i>before</i> the first known personal ad. That&#39;s the premise. Therefore, since the media wouldn&#39;t have been aware of this alleged communication, it&#39;s not relevant when or what they reported.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 436-->
<!--Post: 437--><!--Time: 1089664505-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 12, 2004 - 1:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Also, the newspaper shown on Dateline NBC was the <i>Eagle-Beacon</i> and not the <i>Sun</i>. <BR> <BR>Everyone, please keep in mind that I&#39;m already quite aware what has already been reported as &#34;factual&#34; concerning when and where BTK first communicated. There&#39;s just no point in re-hashing all of that here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 437-->
<!--Post: 438--><!--Time: 1089666599-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST438"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 12, 2004 - 2:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ummmmm, <BR> <BR>Sorry! Just trying to help. <BR> <BR>Jaden<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 438-->
<!--Post: 439--><!--Time: 1089666932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 12, 2004 - 2:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jaden, I appreciate the feedback. I just want everyone to be on the same page in this thread, as it could be quite significant.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 439-->
<!--Post: 458--><!--Time: 1089751041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST458"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, July 13, 2004 - 1:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, I just got word from an awesome source there was no connection between the January 20, 1974 newspaper shown on Dateline and the personal ad to BTK of October 1974. I&#39;ll delete this thread as soon as people have a chance to read the news.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 458-->
